>>
Rule 1 (input tensor must be floating-point)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8
>>
Rule 2 (input tensor must not be boolean to avoid mish_cpu Bool error)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 0
>>
Rule 3 (if the tensor has dimensions, all shape sizes must be positive)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 1
>>
Rule 4 (in-place Mish is only allowed for floating-point inputs)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : bool} |= if v_2 then (dtype_(v_1) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8)
